{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435993-sorcerers-as-a-greater-template","id":1435993,"title":"Sorcerers as a greater template","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-19T05:04:54-08:00","id":1435993,"title":"Sorcerers as a greater template","content":"I happened to reread Chronicles of Darkness The Dark Eras Companion and I happened on something very interesting.<br /> <br /> &quot;The sorcerers described by these systems ultimately represent a half-lost, degenerate tradition. In the time of Irem, sorcerers enjoyed instruction and Sekhem from Shan\u2019iatu princes, mastering mighty spells and the ability to help their masters reliably and more swiftly produce relics. There might once have been some form of greater sorcerer that conferred a true supernatural template, but those days are long passed from this world. Even if it was to be rediscovered this would not confer the kind of \u201cawakening\u201d seen elsewhere, since all sorcery stems not from some numinous higher world, but through living intersections between worldly Sekhem, chthonic powers, and Fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> So what I am wondering is, what would a full-on Sorcerer Supernatural Template look like, and do we think/want to speculate if there are plans to see one being developed in the future of MTC second ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T05:35:39-08:00","id":1435997,"title":"","content":"I would say they would have some access to Utterances and their own ritual magic. Maybe instead of one strong aspect of their soul they have one sacrifices aspect<br /> Of their soul? And relics would be their thang.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T14:44:15-08:00","id":1436081,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea of them being identical to mummies, but more in reverse, more like other monsters. Sekhem 1, pillar spread. A couple of Affinities naturally from the way their Pillars stand. Capacity to learn Utterances. Rather than a Descent, they go through an Ascent as their pillars and Sekhem grows, giving them access to more powerful tiers of Utterances. But that was 1e when such Sorcerers were hunted by the arisen and killed for the diasporic code. Now, it might mess up the balance since Sorcery and immortals are no longer as strongly frowned upon. (Except by certain Judges)<br /> <br /> I'd probably say that such a Sorcerer has 5 pillar points to spend, one affinity, and any 2e merits he wants, with the capacity to raise pillars, Sekhem, and learn Utterances via experience. They can earn reminisce beats like a mummy by understanding the past and their own soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 02-19-2021, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T14:49:39-08:00","id":1436083,"title":"","content":"I have made my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1169608-the-vaettir-modified-template-antagonist\">own version for a Sorcerer template</a> a while ago, which was mostly inspired from the way that magi and sorcerers operated in Mahotsukai no Yome. I hope to revise it a bit so it would fit 2e, but I do like it overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T16:51:25-08:00","id":1436094,"title":"","content":"I am all for a template of people with Sekhem that goes 1 to 10, the five (or maybe more, hmm, hehe) Pillars that go from 1 to 5, Utterances, and maybe even Affinities. <br /> <br /> The current Endless 'template' mostly fit my needs on that but other options, like the one from Cleverest of things or LostLight is totally interesting and awesome to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T09:33:10-08:00","id":1436223,"title":"","content":"If I were to make the Sorcerer's into a full template I would take the rule of three idea and elevate it. They have open rites, closed rites, and to make them a full template again I would give them a third power to complete the theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T11:00:03-08:00","id":1436234,"title":"","content":"To stay in theme of Curses, I'd make every ancient Sorcerer suffer from one. Perhaps contracting one from a Tomb was necessary to unlock magic powers or a ritual of initiation branded one into the Sorcerer's soul. Now, the suffering of living with a Curse generates Pillars or Sekhem that the Sorcerer can use. It would explain why not everyone would jump on getting mystic powers, and would make Sorcerers act in strange ways to compensate for their handicaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T11:17:41-08:00","id":1436238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435993-sorcerers-as-a-greater-template?p=1436234#post1436234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To stay in theme of Curses, I'd make every ancient Sorcerer suffer from one. Perhaps contracting one from a Tomb was necessary to unlock magic powers or a ritual of initiation branded one into the Sorcerer's soul. Now, the suffering of living with a Curse generates Pillars or Sekhem that the Sorcerer can use. It would explain why not everyone would jump on getting mystic powers, and would make Sorcerers act in strange ways to compensate for their handicaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't even thought of a curse to balance them out, but I love that idea. Maybe the polar opposite of Mummies, where their magic SHORTENS their lives somehow? Like their current lifespan is measured by how many Pillar Points they have, and thus the more they use their powers, the shorter their lifespan unless they refill their pillars? It's a trope in some movies and shows, that magic will shorten your life in exchange for power, and would make every full on Sorcerer a flash in the pan, a mayfly, capable of feats comparable to the Arisen, but only one brief life to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-20T12:00:29-08:00","id":1436248,"title":"","content":"The great thing about Curses is that they can be anything. Every Sorcerer can have a different one, inspired by a Relic, Utterance or a Deviant Scar. The last one is from Deviant: the Renegades, and it's great. I'm browsing it right now, and your idea could be modeled by &quot;Deterioration&quot;, &quot;Perilous Variation&quot; or &quot;Genetic Disorder&quot;, just to name a few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}